---
description: Use Qodo skills for coding standards, local review, and pull request finding resolution.
alwaysApply: true
---

Qodo is available through this plugin's skills and the `qodo-managed-tools` MCP server.

- Before implementing, editing, or refactoring code, use the `qodo-get-rules` skill. Reuse rules already retrieved for the same workspace, repository, and task. Apply ERROR rules as requirements. WARNING and RECOMMENDATION rules are advisory.
- At a substantive coding milestone, and before handing off completed work, use the `qodo-review` skill. Do not review every trivial edit.
- When the user asks to resolve Qodo comments already posted on a pull request, use the `qodo-review-resolver` skill.
- For questions about how this codebase is structured or why code is written a certain way, use the `qodo-codebase-wisdom` skill.
- When Qodo tools or the `qodo` CLI are missing, use the `qodo-setup` skill if the user asked to set Qodo up. Otherwise continue the task and say that Qodo was not applied.

Follow each skill's own instructions for MCP versus CLI. `qodo-get-rules` uses the connected `rules-search` tool when it is available. `qodo-review` prefers the Qodo CLI, because that command collects the worktree.
